Maya (Docs): Heads-up: I started two tiny docs PRs to clean up the model-catalog cards for mistral-7b-4q and add updated SDK examples + a bench link: #5123 (catalog card + limits) and #5124 (snippets + migration). Want to coordinate wording before merge.

Priya (ML Eng): Saw #5123. Quick summary from infra runs: the 4-bit quant variant (mistral-7b-4q) is stable up to 3072 tokens in our perf harness. After ~1536 tokens latency climbs non-linearly. Memory footprint is good but we observed degraded throughput at very high batch sizes.

Maya (Docs): Thanks. Can you propose the precise sentence for the card and the JSON field updates? I don't want ambiguous phrasing in the card.

Priya (ML Eng): Suggested card text: "max_sequence_length: 3072 (see compatibility note)" and compatibility note: "Note: 4-bit quantized builds reduce memory but may increase per-token latency for very long sequences (>1536 tokens). Throughput at high batch sizes may be lower than fp16 on some kernels. Quality metrics unchanged in our evaluation." Also add compatibility_tags: ["quant-4bit", "throughput-note"].

Alex (SDK): On #5124 I replaced the old JS generate() snippet. Old example used client.generate() which is legacy. New example demonstrates responses.stream() with incremental rendering and includes an example of injecting tool-calls. Old snippet (remove):

```javascript
// old (do not use)
import Redwood from 'redwood';
const client = new Redwood.Client({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const resp = await client.generate({ model: 'mistral-7b', prompt: 'Tl;dr this article' });
console.log(resp.text);
```

New recommended snippet: 

```javascript
// new: streaming Responses API
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood-ai/sdk';
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const stream = await client.responses.stream({ model: 'mistral-7b-4q' });
await stream.send('Summarize the following in 4 bullets');
for await (const token of stream.iterText()) {
  process.stdout.write(token);
}
await stream.close();
```

Alex (SDK): Also added a short migration note: "Migrate: client.generate(...) -> client.responses.create(...) or client.responses.stream(...). Streaming supports incremental UI updates and tool integration."

Tess (Product): Add a tiny callout on the catalog card about deployment modes. Ops asked whether 4q is available on Dedicated and Private.

Priya (ML Eng): Confirm: 4q is supported on Hosted and Dedicated. For Dedicated/Private, node pools must enable the quant runtime flag and use kernel builds that include the 4-bit kernel. Suggested card line: "Supported deployments: Hosted, Dedicated (requires quant kernel enabled). Private on request."

Sam (Infra): One more infra note: Console enforcement relies on the catalog JSON `max_sequence_length` field. If we bump it to 3072 we must also ship a small migration in the Console config or some customers will have inputs rejected. I can coordinate a hotfix in the Console to read a per-variant flag.

Maya (Docs): Good catch. Priya, can you update the catalog JSON in #5123 to set max_sequence_length=3072 for mistral-7b-4q and include compatibility_tags as Priya suggested? Sam, can you add a Console PR to accept the new field?

Priya (ML Eng): Done on branch. Pushed updated JSON and included the compatibility_tags array.

Sam (Infra): I'll open console PR after we merge docs so we don't get mismatch. Will add a short migration script to the console so existing users keep previous behavior until they opt-in.

Alex (SDK): For #5124 I also added a short footnote under the streaming snippet linking to a public benchmark gist with reproducible commands: https://gist.github.com/redwood-ml/mistral4q-bench (contains seq_len sweep and runner flags). Please make sure that link is permanent.

Maya (Docs): Link looks fine. Chris (bench) usually wants Google Sheets but gists are OK for small runs. Tess, do we need product sign-off on the benchmark link?

Tess (Product): As long as it contains the commands and a short table with the 1536/3072 thresholds, OK. We prefer the public sheet for long-term storage but the gist is fine for now.

Maya (Docs): Quick checklist before merge: (1) JSON max_sequence_length updated? (2) compatibility note wording confirmed? (3) snippet uses RedwoodClient and streaming? (4) bench link canonical? (5) Console PR queued?

Priya (ML Eng): (1) yes; (2) wording above is fine; (3) Alex confirmed; (4) gist created; (5) Sam will open console PR after merge.

Alex (SDK): Added a tiny migration blurb in the docs page: "If your code calls client.generate(...), update to client.responses.create(...) or client.responses.stream(...). See SDK changelog for examples." Also added a single-line example for tool calls.

Maya (Docs): Everything looks good. I'll merge #5123 + #5124 once Sam confirms the Console PR will be created. deploy-bot, can you run a staging deploy after we merge?

deploy-bot: staging deploy scheduled post-merge. I will trigger the build when both PRs land on main.

Sam (Infra): Console PR created: #3007. It reads the variant `max_sequence_length` and falls back to the hard cap while feature flag is off. PTAL.

Maya (Docs): Excellent. Merging both now.

deploy-bot: staging deploy started. Logs: https://ci.internal/builds/8012

Priya (ML Eng): Follow-up: added a footnote in the model card with the reproduce command: `bench-run --model mistral-7b-4q --seq-len 3072 --batch 1`.

Maya (Docs): Footnote added and merged. Thanks all — nice small set of coordinated updates.

Tess (Product): nice! :thumbsup:

Alex (SDK): Cheers.
